# Redirect rules for the static site.
#
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build output directory, but its
# source field matches PATHS ONLY. A scheme+hostname source
# ("https://www.example.com/* ...") is a Netlify feature; Pages ignores such a
# line silently -- no error, no warning, no redirect.
#
# An earlier version of this file carried exactly that rule for www->apex. It
# read correctly in the repo and would have done nothing in production, with
# both hostnames serving the site and splitting the canonical URL.
#
# So www.nearmatch.in -> nearmatch.in is configured at the ZONE level instead,
# as a Cloudflare Redirect Rule (dashboard: Rules -> Redirect Rules):
#
#     If    hostname equals  www.nearmatch.in
#     Then  dynamic redirect to
#           concat("https://nearmatch.in", http.request.uri.path)
#           status 301, preserve query string
#
# Vercel never reads this file; its own redirect lives in website/vercel.json
# and is unaffected.
#
# Path-based rules DO work here and can be added below if the site ever needs
# them, e.g.:
#     /old-page  /new-page  301
